===Etymology 1===
Alteration of earlier {{m|en|light}}, from {{inh|en|enm|lighte}}, from {{der|en|ang|līhtte}}, first and third person singular preterite of {{m|ang|līhtan||to light}}) by analogy with {{m|en|bit}}. More at {{m|en|light}}; compare {{m|en|fit|t=fought|id=fought}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|light||ed-form|t=illuminate; start a fire; etc}}
# {{infl of|en|light||ed-form|t=alight: land, come down on}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1896|author=Florence Merriam Bailey|title=A-birding on a Bronco|page=87|passage={{...}} but finally [the bird] came to the tree and, after edging along falteringly, '''lit''' on a branch above them.}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|US|dialectal}} To [[run]] or [[light]] ([[alight]]).
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1988 April 8|author=Grant Pick|title=Johnny Washington's Life|journal=Chicago Reader|url=https://securesite.chireader.com/cgi-bin/Archive/abridged2.bat?path=1988/880408/WSHNGTN
|passage=With that the kid '''lits''' off down the street, and, what do you know!}}

