===Etymology 2===
From {{der|en|enm|lit}}, {{m|enm|lut}}, from {{der|en|ang|lȳt||little, few}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*lūtilaz||little, small}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lewd-||to cower, hunch over}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|lut||little}}, {{cog|gmh|lützen||to make small or low, decrease}}. More at {{l|en|little}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[little|Little]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[little|Little]].

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|lite}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|en|enm|lit}}, from {{der|en|non|litr||colour, dye, complexion, face, countenance}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wlitiz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*wlitaz||sight, face}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wel-||to see}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|litur||colour}}, {{cog|ang|wlite||brightness, appearance, form, aspect, look, countenance, beauty, splendor, adornment}}, {{cog|ang|wlītan||to gaze, look, observe}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialectal}} [[colour|Colour]]; [[blee]]; [[dye]]; [[stain]].

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|lithouse}}, {{l|en|lit-house}}
* {{l|en|litmus}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{der|en|enm|litten}}, {{m|enm|liten}}, from {{der|en|non|lita||to colour}}, from {{m|non|litr||colour}}. See above.

